Native cropped capture and transparency

Status: DONE
Milestone: Live source-region pixels without browser integration
Dependencies: 01_FOUNDATION
Purpose: Mirror a chosen window through the operating system with bounded work.

Tasks:
- [x] Create native CMake build with application and focused test targets.
- [x] Capture only an explicitly selected source window with Windows Graphics Capture.
- [x] Read back only the selected rectangle at a bounded cadence.
- [x] Implement opacity, sampled color key, tolerance and soft alpha edges.
- [x] Release capture resources on stop and report failure/source unavailability.

Acceptance criteria:
- Matching key colors are transparent; other colors retain correct premultiplied alpha.
- Crop validation handles reversed selections, bounds and invalid geometry.
- No fallback to whole-desktop capture, authentication, persistence or network.
- Synthetic original window produces fresh, correctly cropped frames.

Completion evidence:
- scripts\build.ps1 -Test passed: Release /W4 /WX build, 18 crop/pixel checks
  and 26 native integration checks. Exact native output is build\native-test.txt.
- Actual WGC fixture pixels, source repaint, selected-color alpha and real
  layered-window desktop blending were observed, not just model calculations.
- Initial minimize/restore check failed: queued old-sized animation frames
  incorrectly invalidated the crop. Poll now compares real window geometry and
  drops transient frame-size mismatches; restore and real-resize cases pass.
- OS source-window GPU surface is retained in memory; CPU readback is crop-only.
  No shader pipeline or negligible-GPU-cost claim is made.

Completion log:
- 2026-11-06: Started native first slice.
- 2026-11-06: Completed and locally qualified the native crop/composition pipeline.
